id: migrations/2026-09-30-relationship-core-reconciliation
title: "Relationship Core Reconciliation"
kind: migration-receipt
record_shape: header
status: draft
updated: 2026-09-30
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Codex, reconciling the relationship-core proposal on behalf of the maintainer"

purpose: >
  Record the additive migration from slash-as-relationship language to a
  first-class Relationship record, without rewriting historical records or
  overloading the existing Agency Holarchy Relation, execution relationship,
  or interpersonal template.

signal: >
  The protocol's high-resolution constitutional account already treated
  relationship as structurally first, but its machine-facing surfaces scattered
  relation semantics across URLs, Yawn graph edges, execution contracts,
  partner-oriented intake, Arenas, and unmerged proposals. A slash could be
  read as the relationship itself even though it cannot preserve identity,
  history, participation, policy, or authority.

choice:
  selected: >
    Add Relationship Core 0.1 as an experimental, additive contract: generic
    Relationship, reusable Participation, and directional Relation Address.
    Preserve specialized existing records and correct active slash language.
  rejected:
    - "Treat every slash as parentage or relationship identity."
    - "Expand the interpersonal partner template into the universal primitive."
    - "Overload Agency Holarchy Relation beyond its Yawn-to-Yawn structural role."

what_changed:
  new_contracts:
    - core/relationship.yawn
    - core/participation.yawn
    - core/relation-address.yawn
    - schemas/relationship.v0.1.schema.json
    - schemas/participation.v0.1.schema.json
    - schemas/relation-address.v0.1.schema.json
    - schemas/inference-envelope.v0.1.schema.json
  active_language:
    - "core/entity-and-coupling.yawn now says a slash opens or traverses a Relation Address View."
    - "dave/orientation model and page now distinguish the bot's state from the relation address that opens it."
  profiles_preserved:
    - "Agency Holarchy Relation remains a Structural Relation between Yawns."
    - "Execution Relationship V1 remains the delegate-specific authority contract."
    - "templates/relationship.yawn and question-packets/relationship.yawn remain interpersonal profiles."
  conformance_case:
    - "dave/christianity records a public, source-safe relationship View without inferring Dave's religious identity or beliefs."
    - "Historical sources and represented voices remain non-participants unless a separate participation record establishes present involvement."

compatibility:
  old_paths: "Existing slash-shaped paths remain readable as addresses and Views."
  old_records: "No historical record is rewritten or retyped."
  semantic_change: >
    Active documentation now rejects the claim that the slash glyph or route
    itself is the relationship record. The stable Relationship identity lives
    independently of rendered path syntax.
  historical_context: >
    migrations/2026-09-12-cohere-vocabulary-and-attribution.yawn retains the
    original wording as evidence of the earlier model. This receipt supersedes
    that wording only for active semantics; it does not erase its provenance.

not_changed:
  - "Relationship Core 0.1 does not claim a complete universal human ontology."
  - "It does not make all relationships Yawns."
  - "It does not grant authority, publication, consent, or canonical mutation through a relation address."
  - "It does not make generative inference deterministic; it makes provenance and replay boundaries inspectable."
  - "It does not publish private reflection or infer the beliefs of Dave or any other participant."

rollback: >
  Remove the additive core/schema/fixture/test records and restore the active
  wording from the prior revision. Existing v1 contracts, Agency Holarchy 0.2,
  execution relationships, interpersonal profiles, and historical receipts
  remain intact. Any records created under Relationship Core 0.1 retain their
  source IDs and can be archived rather than silently deleted.

links:
  - adr/0003-relationship-core.md
  - core/relationship.yawn
  - core/participation.yawn
  - core/relation-address.yawn
  - spec/ontology.md
  - spec/holarchy.md
  - dave/christianity/relationship.yawn

proof:
  covers: [signal, choice, what_changed, compatibility, not_changed, rollback]
  tests:
    - tests/relationship-core-v0.1.test.mjs
    - tests/authored-by.test.mjs
    - tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs
  validators:
    - scripts/generate-manifest.mjs
    - scripts/validate-mental-models.mjs
  status: pending-local-validation
